["Pathward Financial is a bank that provides prepaid card, payments and commercial lending services. Revenue (net interest income plus noninterest income) rose 5.1% to $837M in fiscal 2025 (ended Sep 30, 2025). Net interest income rose 2.8% to $512M and noninterest income rose 8.9% to $325M; noninterest expense rose 7.0%, and the provision for credit losses was $56.8M, versus $58.1M.","Net income to common rose 2.0% to $185M, or $7.87 per diluted share, and the efficiency ratio was 66.2% versus 65.0%. Pathward returned $168M through dividends and buybacks."],"highlights":["Revenue rose 5.1% to $837M.","Net interest income rose 2.8%.","Noninterest income rose 8.9% to $325M.","Net income to common rose 2.0% to $185M."],"watch":["Efficiency ratio worsened to 66.2%.","Net interest income depends on interest rates.","Noninterest expense was $554M, up 7.0%.","Credit-loss provision was $56.8M."],"table":[["Total revenue",0.8369,0.7964,1],["Net interest income",0.5118,0.4978],["Noninterest income",0.3251,0.2986],["Noninterest expense",0.5542,0.5177],["Provision for credit losses",0.0568,0.0581],["Other items, net",-0.0029,-0.002],["Pre-tax income",0.2231,0.2186,1],["Income tax",0.0363,0.0341],["Noncontrolling interests",-0.0009,-0.0013],["Preferred dividends & other",-0.0007,0.0017],["Net income to common",0.1852,0.1815,1],["Diluted EPS ($)",7.872589,7.203587,0,"eps"],["Book value per share ($)",37.678882,33.100749,0,"eps"]],"sources":[["Pathward Financial, Inc. Form 10-K filings (SEC EDGAR)","https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0000907471&type=10-K"],["Pathward financial statements (StockAnalysis)","https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/cash/financials/"]]},"video":{"revenueLine":{"cap":"Net interest income was 61% of revenue.","say":"Net interest income made up 61 percent of revenue."},"spotlights":[{"kicker":"Revenue","big":"$837M","sub":"revenue · +5.1%","lines":["Net interest income $512M","Noninterest income $325M"],"cap":"Revenue rose 5.1% to $8